xnu: give ml_io_map and delay C linkage in the Adreno driver

The iokitcpp pass compiles this file as C++, where a plain `extern` declaration
gets the C++ mangled name (_Z9ml_io_mapmm, _Z5delayi) while the kernel defines
both as C symbols, so the first CI run failed on them. Every other Sweet file
that calls C code declares it inside extern "C"; this one did not.

No behaviour change.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
@@ -31,8 +31,12 @@
 #define SWEET_GCC_PA       0x100000ULL
 #define SWEET_GCC_SIZE     0x1f4200
 
+/* 内核里这两个都是 C 符号：C++ 文件不加 extern "C" 会被改名成
+ * _Z9ml_io_mapmm / _Z5delayi，链接期找不到（CI 第一次就挂在这里）。 */
+extern "C" {
 extern vm_offset_t ml_io_map(vm_offset_t phys, vm_size_t size);
 extern void delay(int us);
+}
 
 static uint32_t
 sweet_adreno_rd(volatile void *base, uint32_t off)
